From d916cc7bdf23edfea412d094794cabcbbaaeca9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Carlos Alvarado Martinez <45523697+calvarado2004@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:45:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Capture the first serving graph with a graph-pool cuBLAS
 workspace

PyTorch caches one cuBLAS workspace per handle and stream. capture_forwards
warms every serving graph eagerly inside warmup_storage.transient, so the
first cuBLAS call on the capture stream creates that workspace in transient
storage. The first captured graph then records the transient address in its
split-K GEMM and splitKreduce arguments; the following captures allocate a
workspace from the graph pool, which export records.

Export releases transient storage, so the first graph (the largest prefill
capacity) replays a pointer that no recorded allocation owns. On DeepSeek V4.1
TP4 GB10 at 7f534bb6 with --prefill-chunk-size 8192, prefill8192 wrote to an
unmapped address (Xid 31 FAULT_PDE VIRT_WRITE, CUDA_ERROR_ILLEGAL_ADDRESS on
every rank) for any prompt above 7168 tokens. With chunk 4096 a later recorded
allocation happened to cover the address, so prefill4096 wrote its split-K
partials into storage another allocation owns.

Clear the cached workspaces after the warmups and before the first capture.
---
 ignition/preparation/capture.py | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ignition/preparation/capture.py b/ignition/preparation/capture.py
index ec07f343..e7df7fc1 100644
--- a/ignition/preparation/capture.py
+++ b/ignition/preparation/capture.py
@@ -116,6 +116,12 @@ def capture_forwards(functions, signatures, *, session, device, stream, pool,
                     function()
             stream.synchronize()
             stage.update(advance=1)
+    # PyTorch caches one cuBLAS workspace per handle and stream, and the eager warmups above
+    # created it inside transient storage. The first capture would otherwise bake that address
+    # into its split-K GEMMs and export it unrecorded; later captures already take theirs from
+    # the graph pool. Drop the cached workspaces so every capture allocates its own there.
+    torch.cuda.synchronize(device)
+    torch._C._cuda_clearCublasWorkspaces()
     with phase(progress, label, total=len(names)) as stage:
         for name in names:
             function = compiled.get(name, functions[name])
